{{Interlanguage link|Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|ja|紀伊国造|simple|User:Immanuelle/Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko}} is a [[Kuni no miyatsuko|Kuni no miyatsuko]] that had a uniquely high amount of power similar to the {{Ill|Izumo clan|en||simple|User:Immanuelle/Izumo clan}}.<ref name="mw-2023a">{{Cite web |date=2023-03-10 |title=Kuni no miyatsuko {{!}} 國學院大學デジタルミュージアム |url=https://d-museum.kokugakuin.ac.jp/eos/detail/?id=8839 |access-date=2023-12-02 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230310081317/https://d-museum.kokugakuin.ac.jp/eos/detail/?id=8839 |archive-date=2023-03-10 }}</ref>


The Kinoatai family was responsible for this office. According to the Sendai Kuji Hongi, a historic record, Amenomichine no Mikoto, a descendant of Kami Musubi no Mikoto, was the first to be appointed as Ki no Kuni no Miyatsuko during the reign of Emperor Jinmu. However, Ōnagusahiko is often considered the actual precursor of the {{Interlanguage link|Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|ja|紀伊国造}}.<ref name="mw-2023a" />

They run [[Hinokuma Shrine|Hinokuma Shrine]].<ref name="mw-2023a" /><ref name="web.archive.org-2023">{{Cite web|date=2023-12-16|title=Kinokuninomiyatsuko {{!}} 國學院大學デジタルミュージアム|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216060822/https://d-museum.kokugakuin.ac.jp/eos/detail/?id=8597|access-date=2023-12-16|website=web.archive.org}}</ref> and are the Kuni no miyatsuko of [[Kii Province|Kii Province]].

They descend from {{ill|Amanomichine|ja|天道根命|en|6=simple|7=User:Immanuelle/Amanomichine}}<ref name="web.archive.org-2023" />.

They are believed to be buried at {{ill|Iwase-Senzuka Kofun Cluster|en||simple|User:Immanuelle/Iwase-Senzuka Kofun Cluster }}<ref name="Shiseki">{{cite book|title=(国指定史跡事典) National Historic Site Encyclopedia|last1=Isomura|first1=Yukio|last2=Sakai|first2=Hideya|date=2012|publisher=学生社|isbn=4311750404}}{{in lang|ja}}</ref>.<!-- citation taken from the article, see it for content -->.

They worshipped the daughters of Susanoo.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Encyclopedia of Shinto詳細|url=https://d-museum.kokugakuin.ac.jp/eos/detail/id=9161|access-date=2024-04-01|website=國學院大學デジタルミュージアム|language=ja}}</ref>
