'''Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko''' (紀伊国造) refers to the {{ill|Miyatsuko|ja|国造}} who governed {{ill|Kii Province|ja|紀伊国}} (modern {{ill|Wakayama Prefecture|ja|和歌山県}}). This clan of Miyatsuko descended from the {{ill|Divine Clan|ja|神別}}, specifically the '''Ki-shi''' (紀氏). Historically, they held the dual responsibilities of the office of Miyatsuko in Kii Province and the priestly duties of {{ill|Hinokuma Shrine and Kunikakasu Shrine|ja|日前神宮・國懸神宮}}. Even after the abolition of the Miyatsuko system during the establishment of the {{ill|Ritsuryō system|ja|律令制}}, they retained the title "Miyatsuko" as hereditary priests (宮司) of these shrines.

== Overview ==

=== Name Variants ===
In the {{ill|Sendai Kuji Hongi|ja|先代旧事本紀}}, the name is recorded as 紀伊国造 (Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko). Older texts use variants such as '''Ki no Kuni no Miyatsuko''' (木国造) in the {{ill|Kojiki|ja|古事記}} and '''Ki no Kuni no Miyatsuko''' (紀国造) in the {{ill|Nihon Shoki|ja|日本書紀}}.

