In the {{ill|Meiji period|ja|明治時代}}, the family entered the {{ill|Kazoku|ja|華族}} peerage system, obtaining baronial status. Members served in government roles, such as {{ill|Baron Ki Toshihide|ja|紀俊秀}}, who represented the family in the {{ill|House of Peers|ja|貴族院}}.<ref>{{Cite book|和書|date=2006年（平成18年）|title=華族 近代日本貴族の虚像と実像|author=小田部雄次|authorlink=小田部雄次|publisher=[[中央公論新社]]|series=[[中公新書]]1836|isbn= 978-4121018366|ref=harv}}</ref>

