'''Kinokuno Clan''' (紀氏, ''Ki no Uji'') is a clan whose family name is "Ki."

The Kinokuno Clan was an ancient {{ill|Gōzoku|ja|豪族|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gōzoku|qq=}} based in {{ill|Kinori|ja|紀里|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kinori|qq=}}, Heguri District, Yamato Province (present-day Kamisho, {{ill|Heguri|ja|平群町|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Heguri|qq=}}, Ikoma District, Nara Prefecture). Initially holding the title of {{ill|Omi|ja|臣|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Omi|qq=}}, they were renamed {{ill|Asomi|ja|朝臣|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Asomi|qq=}} under the {{ill|Yatsuka no Kabane|ja|八色の姓|1=Eight Kabane system|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yatsuka no Kabane|13=User:Immanuelle/Eight Kabane system|qq=}} system established in the 13th year of {{ill|Emperor Tenmu|ja|Emperor Tenmu|1=Emperor Tenmu|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Tenmu|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Tenmu|qq=}}'s reign (684 AD).

== Overview ==

According to sources like the {{ill|Nihon Shoki|ja|記紀|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nihon Shoki|qq=}}, the Kinokuno Clan descended from {{ill|Emperor Kōgen|ja|孝元天皇|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Kōgen|qq=}}, with {{ill|Ki no Tsuno|ja|紀角|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Tsuno|qq=}}, a son of {{ill|Takenouchi no Sukune|ja|武内宿禰|1=Takenouchi no Sukune|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takenouchi no Sukune|qq=}}, as their progenitor. Both Ki no Tsuno and his predecessor were maternally descended from the {{ill|Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|ja|紀氏|1=Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|de|Ki (Klan)|uk|Рід Кі|ko|기씨 (황별)|fr|Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|3=紀伊国造|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|13=User:Immanuelle/Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|qq=}} family. This relationship suggests that the clan served the {{ill|Yamato Kingship|ja|ヤマト王権|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yamato Kingship|qq=}} early on as a military house. Figures like {{ill|Ki no Oyu|ja|紀小弓|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Oyu|qq=}}, {{ill|Ki no Oiwashi|ja|紀大磐|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Oiwashi|qq=}}, and {{ill|Ki no Otomaro|ja|紀男麻呂|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Otomaro|qq=}} were active in military and diplomatic affairs, particularly regarding the Korean Peninsula, during the reigns of {{ill|Emperor Yūryaku|ja|雄略天皇|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Yūryaku|qq=}}, {{ill|Emperor Kenzo|ja|顕宗天皇|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Kenzo|qq=}}, and {{ill|Emperor Kinmei|ja|欽明天皇|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Kinmei|qq=}}.

Although the Kinokuno Clan belonged to the Takenouchi lineage, like the {{ill|Katsuragi Clan|ja|葛城氏|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Katsuragi Clan|qq=}}, {{ill|Kose Clan|ja|巨勢氏|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kose Clan|qq=}}, and {{ill|Heguri Clan|ja|平群氏|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Heguri Clan|qq=}}, they notably did not produce a {{ill|Ōomi|ja|大臣|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōomi|qq=}} before the {{ill|Taika Reform|ja|大化の改新|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Taika Reform|qq=}} period.

During the reign of {{ill|Emperor Tenji|ja|天智天皇|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Tenji|qq=}}, {{ill|Ki no Ōtoko|ja|紀大人|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Ōtoko|qq=}} served as the {{ill|Ōtsukasa|ja|御史大夫|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōtsukasa|qq=}}. In the Nara period, {{ill|Ki no Maro|ja|紀麻呂|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Maro|qq=}} became a {{ill|Dainagon|ja|大納言|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Dainagon|qq=}}, {{ill|Ki no Masaru|ja|紀麻路|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Masaru|qq=}} a {{ill|Chūnagon|ja|中納言|1=Chūnagon|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chūnagon|13=User:Immanuelle/Chūnagon|qq=}}, and {{ill|Ki no Iimaro|ja|紀飯麻呂|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Iimaro|qq=}} a {{ill|Sangi|ja|参議|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sangi|qq=}}. The clan flourished as an {{ill|Outer Clan|ja|外戚|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Outer Clan|qq=}} after {{ill|Prince Shirakabe|ja|白壁王|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Prince Shirakabe|qq=}}, born to {{ill|Ki no Tsuji Hime|ja|紀橡姫|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Tsuji Hime|qq=}} and {{ill|Prince Shiki|ja|志貴皇子|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Prince Shiki|qq=}}, ascended as {{ill|Emperor Kōnin|ja|光仁天皇|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Kōnin|qq=}}. However, during the {{ill|Heian period|ja|平安時代|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Heian period|qq=}}, the clan's influence waned due to the rise of the {{ill|Fujiwara Hokke|ja|藤原北家|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fujiwara Hokke|qq=}}.

By the early Heian period, only a few members, such as {{ill|Ki no Haseo|ja|紀長谷雄|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Haseo|qq=}}, managed to hold significant positions. They later transitioned to literary contributions, producing figures like {{ill|Ki no Tsurayuki|ja|紀貫之|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Tsurayuki|qq=}}, {{ill|Ki no Tomonori|ja|紀友則|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Tomonori|qq=}}, and {{ill|Ki no Tokifumi|ja|紀時文|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Tokifumi|qq=}}.

