'''Kinokuno Clan''' (紀氏, ''Ki no Uji'') is a clan whose family name is "Ki."

The Kinokuno Clan was an ancient [[:en:Gōzoku|Gōzoku]] based in {{ill|Kinori|ja|紀里|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kinori|qq=}}, Heguri District, Yamato Province (present-day Kamisho, [[:en:Heguri, Nara|Heguri]], Ikoma District, Nara Prefecture). Initially holding the title of [[:en:Omi (title)|Omi]], they were renamed [[:en:Ason|Asomi]] under the {{ill|Yatsuka no Kabane|ja|八色の姓|1=Eight Kabane system|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yatsuka no Kabane|13=User:Immanuelle/Eight Kabane system|qq=}} system established in the 13th year of {{ill|Emperor Tenmu|ja|Emperor Tenmu|1=Emperor Tenmu|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Tenmu|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Tenmu|qq=}}'s reign (684 AD).

== Overview ==

According to sources like the {{ill|Nihon Shoki|ja|記紀|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nihon Shoki|qq=}}, the Kinokuno Clan descended from [[:en:Emperor Kōgen|Emperor Kōgen]], with {{ill|Ki no Tsuno|ja|紀角|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Tsuno|qq=}}, a son of [[:en:Takenouchi no Sukune|Takenouchi no Sukune]], as their progenitor. Both Ki no Tsuno and his predecessor were maternally descended from the {{ill|Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|ja|紀氏|1=Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|de|Ki (Klan)|uk|Рід Кі|ko|기씨 (황별)|fr|Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|3=紀伊国造|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|13=User:Immanuelle/Kii no Kuni no Miyatsuko|qq=}} family. This relationship suggests that the clan served the [[:en:Yamato Kingship|Yamato Kingship]] early on as a military house. Figures like {{ill|Ki no Oyu|ja|紀小弓|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Oyu|qq=}}, {{ill|Ki no Oiwashi|ja|紀大磐|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Oiwashi|qq=}}, and {{ill|Ki no Otomaro|ja|紀男麻呂|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Otomaro|qq=}} were active in military and diplomatic affairs, particularly regarding the Korean Peninsula, during the reigns of [[:en:Emperor Yūryaku|Emperor Yūryaku]], [[:en:Emperor Kenzō|Emperor Kenzo]], and [[:en:Emperor Kinmei|Emperor Kinmei]].

Although the Kinokuno Clan belonged to the Takenouchi lineage, like the [[:en:Katsuragi clan|Katsuragi Clan]], {{ill|Kose Clan|ja|巨勢氏|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kose Clan|qq=}}, and {{ill|Heguri Clan|ja|平群氏|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Heguri Clan|qq=}}, they notably did not produce a [[:en:Minister (government)|Ōomi]] before the [[:en:Taika Reform|Taika Reform]] period.

During the reign of [[:en:Emperor Tenji|Emperor Tenji]], {{ill|Ki no Ōtoko|ja|紀大人|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Ōtoko|qq=}} served as the {{ill|Ōtsukasa|ja|御史大夫|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōtsukasa|qq=}}. In the Nara period, {{ill|Ki no Maro|ja|紀麻呂|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Maro|qq=}} became a [[:en:Dainagon|Dainagon]], {{ill|Ki no Masaru|ja|紀麻路|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Masaru|qq=}} a [[:en:Chūnagon|Chūnagon]], and {{ill|Ki no Iimaro|ja|紀飯麻呂|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Iimaro|qq=}} a [[:en:Sangi (Japan)|Sangi]]. The clan flourished as an [[:en:Consort kin|Outer Clan]] after {{ill|Prince Shirakabe|ja|白壁王|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Prince Shirakabe|qq=}}, born to {{ill|Ki no Tsuji Hime|ja|紀橡姫|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ki no Tsuji Hime|qq=}} and [[:en:Prince Shiki|Prince Shiki]], ascended as [[:en:Emperor Kōnin|Emperor Kōnin]]. However, during the [[:en:Heian period|Heian period]], the clan's influence waned due to the rise of the [[:en:Fujiwara Hok-ke|Fujiwara Hokke]].

By the early Heian period, only a few members, such as [[:en:Ki no Haseo|Ki no Haseo]], managed to hold significant positions. They later transitioned to literary contributions, producing figures like [[:en:Ki no Tsurayuki|Ki no Tsurayuki]], [[:en:Ki no Tomonori|Ki no Tomonori]], and [[:en:Ki no Tokibumi|Ki no Tokifumi]].

